# Wave W17-Q (Route 121): standing stones — a pair of pilgrim-track standing stones beside the road to Mt. Requiem: two grey uprights of different heights, moss creeping at their feet, the stones the pilgrim talks to the whole way (design: the pilgrim walks to the mountain twice a year and talks to the stones the whole way — they answer in their own time). On warden turf (fully opaque, ground baked in) — split from Route 39’s stacked hill cairn by form: these stones stand, they are not piled.
